---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About Taxfold"
  description="Who makes Taxfold, the local-only receipt and expense log for iPhone, and who writes the guides on taxfold.app."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">About Taxfold</h1>

    <p>
      Taxfold is a receipt and expense log for iPhone, made by Opal Harmony P.C., a small software company in Greece.
      It is in development and not yet on the App Store.
    </p>

    <h2>Why local-only</h2>
    <p>
      A box of receipts is a record of where you shop, what you earn from and who you work with. Taxfold keeps that
      record on your phone: there is no account to create, no server that holds a copy and no bank connection. When
      you need the receipts somewhere else, you export them yourself. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> says
      exactly what the app and this website collect.
    </p>

    <h2>The guides</h2>
    <p>
      The guides on this site explain how to keep, organise and hand over receipts and expense records. They are
      signed by the <strong>Taxfold team</strong> at Opal Harmony P.C., which builds the app. A person on the team
      reviews every page before it is published. <a href="/how-we-write/">How we write the guides</a> describes the process,
      including where AI tools are used.
    </p>
    <p>
      The guides are general information, not tax, legal or accounting advice. Tax rules differ by country and change
      over time; check anything you rely on with your tax authority or an accountant.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href="mailto:hello@taxfold.app">hello@taxfold.app</a> with questions, corrections or anything else.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
